{"evt":"summary_set","id":"note:note-mqq1rh9jnxp","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","summary":"OBSERVED (2026-06-22, feature bench-prod-parity, N=2): an impl worker running >10min gets its claim auto-released by the stale-claim reaper (\"auto-released: worker 'X' not running (stale >10m)\"), and the subsequent late `tested` completion does NOT propagate readiness to the blocking judge task — the judge stays not_ready (P1: 13.5min run → judge stuck not_ready). A worker finishing <10min completes cleanly and its judge auto-readies on `tested` (P2: 5min run → judge went ready). So the 10-min reaper threshold is too aggressive for multi-minute impl workers, AND the late-completion transition skips dependent-ready propagation (likely because the claim lease is already gone when `complete` fires, so the transition handler takes a path that doesn't re-derive dependents). SEPARATE GOTCHA confirmed same session: raw merge_attempt does the git merge ONLY — the impl must additionally be set_status done to release its impl-dependents; the judge's submit_verdict bundles merge+done, the raw escape hatch does not. FIX DIRECTION (candidate task P7): (a) raise/disable the stale threshold while a worker is actively progressing (heartbeat or longer TTL), and (b) re-run dependent-readiness derivation on the `tested` transition regardless of claim-lease state.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-23T02:59:35.295Z"}
